  "body": "Right now the only way to tell which SyntaxError is being referenced is to hover over the type name and look at the URL.\n\nI would personally prefer the following pattern:\n\n> Throw a [`DOMException`](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#dfn-DOMException) \"[`SyntaxError`](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#syntaxerror)\"\n\nand I would prefer changing this across the entire document for all DOMExceptions.\n\nWhat do people think?\n",
